1
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:08,940
=When the Lights Rise=
=Episode 3=

2
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:16,920
This is...

3
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:01,560
Watch out!

4
00:02:17,960 --> 00:02:19,400
(What's this woman's name?)

5
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,160
Where does she live?

6
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:22,360
I don't know her name.

7
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,240
She's in her twenties.

8
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:25,840
Her hair was tied up,

9
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,320
and she wore a floral qipao.

10
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:31,360
She was spotted near
the Mei family's tailor shop.

11
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,320
The French Concession.

12
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,680
It was only after Mei Xiaozhu died

13
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,720
that I made the connection.

14
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,080
How did you make that connection?

15
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:42,880
Through my contacts in the Kun Society.

16
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:44,880
Do you want to know about those too?

17
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:05,640
Thank you.

18
00:03:11,040 --> 00:03:12,560
That woman who just tried to kill you,

19
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:13,920
do you know her?

20
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,520
No.

21
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,360
Then did your sister, Mei Xiaozhu,

22
00:03:18,080 --> 00:03:20,040
have an older female friend
she was close to?

23
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,160
What do you mean?

24
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,000
On August 1,

25
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:27,360
she came to borrow money from me.

26
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:28,360
As a rule,

27
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:30,280
I never lend money to students.

28
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,960
I don't want them
chasing unrealistic dreams

29
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:32,880
and indulging in pleasure

30
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,120
at the expense of their studies.

31
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,320
But she told me

32
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,880
she needed to help her older friend

33
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,240
who was facing a family crisis

34
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,280
and urgently needed money.

35
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,520
That, I could understand.

36
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,320
Besides, she was the top student
at Mintong Middle School.

37
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,480
A good school and an excellent student.

38
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:49,520
Surely she wouldn't be
like those modern young people

39
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:52,000
who've completely lost their senses.

40
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:03,800
I originally thought

41
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:05,680
she borrowed the money to help you.

42
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:10,000
But since you're not
the woman she mentioned,

43
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:12,120
who was this older friend she spoke of?

44
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:13,320
(Student ID)

45
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:16,240
And who was the woman
who just tried to kill you?

46
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:22,440
There is no other older friend.

47
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,080
I'm her only sister.

48
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:26,040
I heard

49
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:29,080
she met a woman
a few years older than her

50
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,360
who worked as
a dance hostess on Fourth Road.

51
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,880
I know you're here for the money.

52
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,080
Take it and leave.

53
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:47,000
This tailor shop isn't safe anymore.

54
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,400
I happen to know a place

55
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:51,640
where your sister can stay for now.

56
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,960
I'm a debt collector.

57
00:04:54,320 --> 00:04:55,120
Money is all I care about.

58
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,040
I don't kill people.

59
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:58,520
There's no need
to be so hostile toward me.

60
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:00,480
I've already told you.

61
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:01,440
Pay now,

62
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,680
and I'll waive half the interest.

63
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:04,240
You've overpaid. Here's the extra.

64
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:05,360
I'm giving you this money

65
00:05:05,520 --> 00:05:06,880
because you saved my life just now,

66
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,520
not to repay Xiaozhu's debt.

67
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:11,000
She would never borrow money
behind my back.

68
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,800
I know you don't want
to draw any conclusions yet.

69
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,120
Because acknowledging the debt

70
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:24,240
would mean

71
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,120
accepting everything you've seen so far.

72
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:27,960
But in this hot weather,

73
00:05:28,640 --> 00:05:29,960
your sister can't stay here

74
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:31,840
until the truth comes to light.

75
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:34,320
Wait.

76
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,560
That place you mentioned,

77
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,200
where is it?

78
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,160
These courtesans
all worked on Fourth Road.

79
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:09,680
When someone in their profession
passes away,

80
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:10,880
the others collect some money

81
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,800
to hold a memorial service here.

82
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,440
I'm afraid your sister
will have to make do.

83
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,280
This is the only place
that can take her in right now.

84
00:06:19,840 --> 00:06:20,760
While we're alive,

85
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,320
people are always divided
into different social classes.

86
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,760
But in death, everyone is equal.

87
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:28,960
Rather than this false sense of dignity,

88
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:32,960
I'd rather know the truth.

89
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:35,360
Exactly.

90
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,600
Once you're dead, you're dead.

91
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,960
Whether the dead rest in peace

92
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:43,360
is just something
the living tell themselves.

93
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,240
Have you made any funeral arrangements?

94
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,160
I want her cremated.

95
00:07:07,640 --> 00:07:08,440
Cremated?

96
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,520
Xiaozhu once said

97
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,960
that if she died,

98
00:07:15,840 --> 00:07:16,880
she wanted to be cremated.

99
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,160
I didn't understand it back then.

100
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,400
But seeing her like this now,

101
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:23,680
there's really no need

102
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,040
to take this body into the next life.

103
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:28,680
Better to turn to ashes

104
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,040
and leave everything behind.

105
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:34,240
Perhaps that's a better way to rest.

106
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,000
Xiaozhu.

107
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,160
I will always believe you.

108
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:48,440
Miss Mei.

109
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:50,640
In the eyes of the world,

110
00:07:51,240 --> 00:07:53,440
an autopsy violates
the dignity of the dead.

111
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:55,040
She's your own sister.

112
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,360
How could you bring yourself to do it?

113
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,640
She's the one who asked me to.

114
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:03,640
She said her body was the answer.

115
00:08:04,120 --> 00:08:04,920
What does that mean?

116
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,200
I found this in her stomach.

117
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:15,240
Coca leaves?

118
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:16,360
You know what these are?

119
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,640
They're used to make cocaine.

120
00:08:17,680 --> 00:08:18,880
Cocaine?

121
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:20,560
A drug similar to opium.

122
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,480
Are you saying

123
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,560
Xiaozhu was taking drugs?

124
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,120
Bluish ears

125
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:27,520
and deep red lips

126
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,240
are signs of an overdose.

127
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,000
Impossible.

128
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,640
She's just a student.

129
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,360
How could she have gotten hold
of something like that?

130
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:37,680
Could she have eaten it by mistake?

131
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:40,320
Don't all these leaves look alike?

132
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:41,960
Accidentally eating it once
would make sense.

133
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,320
But judging by her condition,

134
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,840
she was exposed to quite a large amount.

135
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,640
Perhaps her death

136
00:08:49,040 --> 00:08:50,720
was caused by hallucinations

137
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,400
from a cocaine overdose.

138
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:53,520
Hallucinations?

139
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,000
I once had a debtor

140
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:56,440
who took an overdose

141
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:57,760
and wandered into a racetrack,

142
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:58,960
where he was trampled
to death by a horse.

143
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:04,320
But if she only wanted to die,

144
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:07,760
why would she reach for the chandelier?

145
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,760
Could she have

146
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:17,120
seen something in her hallucinations?

147
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:24,880
I have to save her.

148
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:26,480
I have to save her.

149
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:28,440
I have to save her.

150
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:34,320
No.

151
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,240
You're wrong.

152
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,680
This wasn't some hallucination
or accident.

153
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:39,960
This was murder.

154
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:41,840
Whoever gave her access to coca leaves

155
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:43,480
is the real killer.

156
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:45,920
Mother, come to your senses.

157
00:09:45,950 --> 00:09:46,900
Mother!

158
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:49,120
Mother, you can't sell me.

159
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,240
You can't sell our home.

160
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,120
Mother!

161
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:52,760
If she doesn't sell you,

162
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:55,200
how will she pay off
all those debts from her indulgences?

163
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:57,120
Let go of me!

164
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:58,960
Mother, come to your senses!

165
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,880
Mother, please come to your senses!

166
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:01,880
Mother!

167
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:02,800
Mr. Ding.

168
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,120
Mr. Ding.

169
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,720
You know a lot of people.

170
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,320
Could you help me find out

171
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:08,760
whose supply it came from?

172
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:19,060
Newspapers!

173
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:20,780
Newspapers!

174
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,800
Are you taking me to an opium den?

175
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,440
Do they have coca leaves there?

176
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,080
If you want information about that,

177
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:29,600
we should start with someone
who sells opium residue.

178
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:30,960
Opium residue?

179
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,600
This is opium residue.

180
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:42,760
It's what's left after smoking opium.

181
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:43,840
Add some water and boil it again,

182
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,720
and you can extract a little more.

183
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:47,320
Then it's sold to addicts
who can't afford better.

184
00:10:47,800 --> 00:10:48,960
After they've smoked the residue,

185
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,480
what's left is opium water.

186
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,760
Even that can be sold again.

187
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,440
People actually buy this?

188
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:56,400
No matter how poor someone is,

189
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:58,960
the addiction doesn't just go away.

190
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:00,960
Even a little relief
is better than none.

191
00:11:01,480 --> 00:11:02,960
Wouldn't you agree, Boss Ding?

192
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,120
Let me ask you something.

193
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:04,960
Go ahead.

194
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,040
I know all those opium addicts

195
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:08,280
who owe you money.

196
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,960
Have you heard of coca leaves?

197
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:11,480
What?

198
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:13,040
They're used to make cocaine.

199
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,160
It's a fashionable drug
in the concessions.

200
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:18,040
I've heard of heroin.

201
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:19,600
Is it the same thing?

202
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:20,400
More or less.

203
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,400
Can you buy it around here?

204
00:11:22,800 --> 00:11:25,120
Is it made by boiling
something like this?

205
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:29,360
That's something for the wealthy.

206
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:30,840
How would I ever get my hands on it?

207
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,700
Why don't you try

208
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:35,480
the new opium den on Minguo Road

209
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:36,520
and ask around?

210
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,760
A newly opened opium den?

211
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,360
Is it licensed by the government?

212
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:44,760
The license was obtained
by the Kuang family's illegitimate son.

213
00:11:45,200 --> 00:11:47,080
Now they can sell opium openly.

214
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:49,000
The place is incredibly luxurious.

215
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:49,960
I'm sure

216
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,480
they have the leaves
you're talking about.

217
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,200
The illegitimate son he mentioned

218
00:11:54,400 --> 00:11:55,320
is Lv Mengde.

219
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,520
That man has no principles.

220
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,200
He's working with the Japanese

221
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:02,640
and has cut off all
our business connections.

222
00:12:05,400 --> 00:12:07,320
Since when do opium dealers care
about principles?

223
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:13,880
Need a rickshaw?

224
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:21,180
(Opium Den)

225
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,200
Hey, beautiful.

226
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:47,800
Come on in.

227
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,140
(Jinpeng Opium Den)

228
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:01,840
Anyone here?

229
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:04,360
Anyone here?

230
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,200
Follow me.

231
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,000
Oh, dear.

232
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:45,040
Mother, you can't sell me.

233
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:46,520
You can't sell our home.

234
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:47,600
Come to your senses!

235
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:48,760
Mother!

236
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:10,720
Give it to me.

237
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:12,480
Do you want me dead?

238
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,240
Smoking opium is what's
going to kill you.

239
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:16,960
Give it to me!

240
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:20,590
Give it to me!

241
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,280
Zhao, I want Mother.

242
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:23,680
Please don't lock Mother up.

243
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:26,520
Zhao, don't lock Mother up.

244
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:29,440
What are you doing?

245
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:44,480
Mother, wake up!

246
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:47,560
Mother, wake up!

247
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:48,840
Wake up!

248
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:50,680
Mother, wake up!

249
00:14:52,920 --> 00:14:53,720
Mr. Ding.

250
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:54,640
What's wrong?

251
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:57,800
Are you all right?

252
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,040
I'm fine.

253
00:15:01,720 --> 00:15:03,320
Why don't you step outside for a moment?

254
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:04,480
I'll find someone to ask.

255
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:10,760
You were right.

256
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:14,400
They're the real killers.

257
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:16,680
Welcome.

258
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,520
How can I help you two?

259
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:20,880
Are you the owner?

260
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:21,690
Yes.

261
00:15:25,080 --> 00:15:26,200
Oh, we...

262
00:15:26,920 --> 00:15:29,560
We've just received
a shipment of premium opium.

263
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,200
Would you like to try some?

264
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:34,080
We're not here to smoke opium.

265
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:36,360
We're looking for coca leaves.

266
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,200
Cocaine.

267
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:38,280
Do you have any?

268
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:39,000
Yes,

269
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:39,840
of course.

270
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,440
Just a moment.

271
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,560
Here it is.

272
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,160
Let me tell you,

273
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:56,080
this is an exclusive supply.

274
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:57,480
You won't find it

275
00:15:57,480 --> 00:15:59,440
anywhere else on the market.

276
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:03,000
Isn't this the kind of injection
they give at foreign clinics?

277
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,200
Ah, you don't understand.

278
00:16:05,720 --> 00:16:07,360
The injections at foreign clinics

279
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:08,840
are meant to heal the body.

280
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,560
This one heals the soul.

281
00:16:12,200 --> 00:16:13,120
Just one injection,

282
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:14,920
and you'll feel like
you're floating in paradise,

283
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,200
completely carried away.

284
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,600
We want edible coca leaves.

285
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,360
Do you have those?

286
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:20,720
Coca leaves?

287
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:23,080
This is injected,

288
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:23,920
not eaten.

289
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:25,040
Do you have coca leaves?

290
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:29,200
We've seen them ourselves.

291
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:31,000
Something you can swallow.

292
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:33,560
Something you can swallow?

293
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,880
Oh, you mean coca wine,

294
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:36,560
right?

295
00:16:36,800 --> 00:16:37,880
Coca wine?

296
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:38,920
Yes.

297
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:42,110
♪And watch the lights
come on one by one♪

298
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:45,510
♪Like blades cutting
through the radiance♪

299
00:16:46,160 --> 00:16:49,070
♪You may treat me as dust
beneath your feet♪

300
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:50,910
♪Or wipe me away like ashes♪

301
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,630
♪Leaving a cold ending♪

302
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:54,430
♪But I refuse to fall♪

303
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:59,070
♪I refuse to become a shadow
fading beneath the lights♪

304
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:02,390
♪I refuse to dissolve into♪

305
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,980
♪The lifeless light of the past♪

306
00:17:06,330 --> 00:17:09,150
♪I want sharpness at my fingertips♪

307
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:11,970
♪And steps that avoid
the traps among the thorns♪

308
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:15,590
♪At dawn, I will look
straight into your eyes♪

309
00:17:15,590 --> 00:17:18,790
♪My gaze clear, illuminating the dawn♪

310
00:17:20,480 --> 00:17:23,030
♪Those who have hurt me♪

311
00:17:23,590 --> 00:17:26,270
♪I choose to pierce through♪

312
00:17:27,720 --> 00:17:29,590
♪To tear apart♪

313
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:35,230
♪To ignite a sacred flame♪

314
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:39,150
♪I do not pray to the gods♪

315
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:42,230
♪Nor bow to power♪

316
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:44,270
♪I will no longer play the tragic lead♪

317
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:50,310
♪I will stand and carve
the path of my own fate♪
